    "result_text": "Owner responses now include `membershipTier`. It's `\"SILVER\"` when the owner's `namesakeCount` is 0 and they have an email, and `\"BRONZE\"` otherwise. I ran the test suite and it passes: both tests in the repo (the two acceptance tests for this rule) succeed.\n\nThe change touches two files:\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**: added `membershipTier` to the `Owner` schema as a read-only string, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`**: added a `toMembershipTier(owner)` method, mapped onto `membershipTier` in the same way as the existing `membershipNumber`.\n\nTwo choices of mine go slightly beyond the spec:\n- An email that is blank or only spaces counts as \"no email\", so that owner gets `BRONZE`.\n- An owner with no stored `namesakeCount` also gets `BRONZE`.\n\nThe tier isn't stored; it's worked out each time an owner is returned, so it also updates when the email or `namesakeCount` changes later.",
